What is an API Contract?

An API Contract is an agreement between the API Provider (Backend) and the API Consumer (Frontend, Mobile App, or another Service).

Think of it like a contract between a customer and a restaurant.

Restaurant Contract:

Customer orders food.
Restaurant prepares the food.
Restaurant returns the food.
If the item is unavailable, the restaurant informs the customer.

Both sides know what to expect.

The same idea applies to APIs.

Example

Imagine you're building a Jewellery website.

Frontend

The React application wants product details.

It sends:

GET /products/10

The backend understands:

"The customer wants product ID 10."

The backend responds:

{
    "id":10,
    "name":"Gold Ring",
    "price":25000
}

This response format is part of the API Contract.

