Why API Contracts are Important?

Imagine the frontend developer expects

{
   "id":10,
   "name":"Ring",
   "price":25000
}

But the backend sends

{
   "productId":10,
   "productName":"Ring",
   "amount":25000
}

The frontend will fail because the agreed structure changed.

That's why both teams agree on the contract before development.

